[{"start": 0.0, "end": 76.72, "text": "What the f***?! Could 38-year-old Steph Curry outshoot the English archers at the Battle of Agincourt? Except these guys were the deadliest shooters of the Middle Ages. Saturday night, Curry dropped 41 on Orlando, 13 of 19, 10 for 10 from the line, in overtime. He's also the only player in NBA history with 4,000 made threes. Meanwhile, October 25th, 1415, a muddy field in northern France. Thousands of English longbowmen, each firing about 10 arrows a minute. So Curry time travels to the front line. One ball, one hoop, no shot clock. The archers fire the first volley. The sky goes dark. Curry pulls up from 200 yards. Splash! Night night, the French Knights charge through the mud. Curry hits a step-back over a horse, and one. The archers adjust. Volley after volley. Curry answers every one. Splash! Night night. At halftime, two monks on the studio desk call it the greatest shooting display of the 15th century. Final volley. Curry slips in the mud, falls backwards, and banks it in anyway. Final score, Curry 213, archers zero. Arrows don't count without a hoop. King Henry knights him on the spot. Sir Stephen still has to be home by tip-off.", "words": [[0.0, "What"], [0.28, "the"], [0.5, "f***?!"], [1.2, "Could"], [1.3, "38-year-old"], [2.16, "Steph"], [2.48, "Curry"], [2.86, "outshoot"], [3.38, "the"], [3.58, "English"], [3.9, "archers"], [4.28, "at"], [4.46, "the"], [4.58, "Battle"], [4.8, "of"], [5.02, "Agincourt?"], [5.88, "Except"], [6.12, "these"], [6.48, "guys"], [6.72, "were"], [6.98, "the"], [7.12, "deadliest"], [7.58, "shooters"], [7.98, "of"], [8.2, "the"], [8.34, "Middle"], [8.48, "Ages."], [9.54, "Saturday"], [9.66, "night,"], [10.4, "Curry"], [10.48, "dropped"], [10.8, "41"], [11.4, "on"], [11.82, "Orlando,"], [12.74, "13"], [13.2, "of"], [13.5, "19,"], [14.44, "10"], [14.74, "for"], [14.94, "10"], [15.26, "from"], [15.46, "the"], [15.6, "line,"], [16.16, "in"], [16.36, "overtime."], [17.52, "He's"], [17.74, "also"], 